::ENG3_U05_L02_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG3.V.02] Sentence: The inscription on the monument clarified the event being remembered. The root script means write. What does inscription most likely mean? {
~A spoken performance#The root points to writing, not speaking.
~A hidden emotion#The context and root do not support this meaning.
=Words written or carved on a surface#Correct. The root script and monument context support this meaning.
~A person who studies monuments#This meaning is not supported by the root or context.
}
::ENG3_U05_L02_GP_Q02::[MLA.ENG3.V.02] Sentence: The final phrase was barely audible. Related word: audio. What does audible mean? {
~Able to be carried#That meaning connects to port, not audio.
=Able to be heard#Correct. Audio relates to sound, and the context supports hearing.
~Able to be seen#That meaning connects to vis or vision.
~Able to be trusted#That meaning connects to credible or credibility.
}
::ENG3_U05_L02_GP_Q03::[MLA.ENG3.V.02] Word family: portable, transport, import, export. What meaning does the root port suggest? {
=Carry or move#Correct. The related words all connect to carrying or moving.
~See or look#That meaning connects to vis.
~Write or mark#That meaning connects to script.
~Hear or sound#That meaning connects to audio.
}
::ENG3_U05_L02_GP_Q04::[MLA.ENG3.R.10] Sentence: The critic questioned the credibility of the source. Word family: credible, credit, incredible. Which paraphrase is best? {
~The critic questioned the color of the source.#This does not match the word family or sentence context.
~The critic questioned where the source was printed.#This adds a detail not in the sentence.
~The critic questioned whether the source was old.#This is not the meaning of credibility.
=The critic questioned whether the source could be trusted.#Correct. Credibility connects to trust or believability.
}
::ENG3_U05_L02_GP_Q05::[MLA.ENG3.V.01] Context: Choose the sentence that uses the derived word visible correctly. {
~The visible of the argument was difficult to hear.#Visible is used incorrectly as a noun.
~The source visible the claim with evidence.#Visible cannot be used as a verb here.
=The speaker made the problem visible by giving a clear example.#Correct. Visible means able to be seen or understood.
~The visible audience listened carefully.#This use is awkward and does not fit the intended meaning.
}
